<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="idb98a3337-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8" identifier="/us/usc/t18/s3102"><ns0:num value="3102">§ 3102.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Authority to issue search warrant—(Rule)</ns0:heading><ns0:note id="idb98a3338-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:heading style="-uslm-lc:I71" class="centered"><ns0:inline class="small-caps">See Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure</ns0:inline></ns0:heading>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0 fontsize7">Federal, State or Territorial Judges, or U.S. magistrate judges authorized to issue search warrants, Rule 41(a).</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
<ns0:sourceCredit id="idb98a3339-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">(<ns0:ref href="/us/act/1948-06-25/ch645">June 25, 1948, ch. 645</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/62/819">62 Stat. 819</ns0:ref>; <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/90/578/tIII/s301/a/4">Pub. L. 90–578, title III, § 301(a)(4)</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1968-10-17">Oct. 17, 1968</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/82/1115">82 Stat. 1115</ns0:ref>; <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/101/650/tIII/s321">Pub. L. 101–650, title III, § 321</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1990-12-01">Dec. 1, 1990</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/104/5117">104 Stat. 5117</ns0:ref>.)</ns0:sourceCredit>
<ns0:notes type="uscNote" id="idb98a333a-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" role="crossHeading" topic="editorialNotes" id="idb98a333b-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered"><ns0:b>Editorial Notes</ns0:b></ns0:heading></ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="amendments" id="idb98a333c-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Amendments</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">1968—<ns0:ref href="/us/pl/90/578">Pub. L. 90–578</ns0:ref> substituted “magistrates” for “Commissioners”.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" role="crossHeading" topic="statutoryNotes" id="idb98a333d-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered"><ns0:b>Statutory Notes and Related Subsidiaries</ns0:b></ns0:heading></ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I78" topic="changeOfName" id="idb98a333e-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Change of Name</ns0:heading>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">“U.S. magistrate judges” substituted for “U.S. magistrates” in text pursuant to <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/101/650/s321">section 321 of Pub. L. 101–650</ns0:ref>, set out as a note under <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t28/s631">section 631 of Title 28</ns0:ref>, Judiciary and Judicial Procedure.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="effectiveDateOfAmendment" id="idb98a333f-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Effective Date of 1968 Amendment</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Amendment by <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/90/578">Pub. L. 90–578</ns0:ref> effective <ns0:date date="1968-10-17">Oct. 17, 1968</ns0:date>, except when a later effective date is applicable, which is the earlier of date when implementation of amendment by appointment of magistrates [now United States magistrate judges] and assumption of office takes place or third anniversary of enactment of <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/90/578">Pub. L. 90–578</ns0:ref> on <ns0:date date="1968-10-17">Oct. 17, 1968</ns0:date>, see <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/90/578/s403">section 403 of Pub. L. 90–578</ns0:ref>, set out as a note under <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t28/s631">section 631 of Title 28</ns0:ref>, Judiciary and Judicial Procedure.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
</ns0:notes>
</ns0:section>
